                  <div style={{ marginTop:"6px" }}>Base rates are top step on a 2,912-hour basis. Where an agency publishes both a 56-hour and a 40-hour rate for the same rank, the 56-hour line rate is used. Where the rank has a paramedic class of its own — El Dorado Hills' Engineer/Paramedic and Captain/Paramedic — that class is used and the Medic column reads $0, because the premium is already inside base pay.</div>
